## Design notes

- **Deadline in monotonic time.** Computing `deadline = t1 + remaining` once means each tick is just `deadline - performance.now()`. Changing the system clock mid-exam has no effect.
- **`Date.now()` appears only as a sleep detector.** If it disagrees with `performance.now()` by more than 2 seconds, the code resyncs. A false positive (say, the student changes their clock) costs one extra request and nothing else.
- **A failed sync never falls back to the device clock.** The timer keeps running from the last good deadline and shows a warning. If the very first sync fails, the exam doesn't start.
- **Zero triggers a confirmation sync.** If an instructor granted extra time while the exam was running, the timer picks it up instead of auto-submitting early.
- **Throttled background tabs** may fire timeouts late, but that doesn't matter because the displayed time is recomputed from the deadline on every tick. The `visibilitychange` resync covers the rest.
- **Keep the server grace window.** The auto-submit at zero arrives a few hundred milliseconds after the deadline, so the 5-second grace on the server prevents on-time students from being marked late.

