I don't know your stack or schema, so I've assumed TypeScript and a ride record shape (below). Adjust the field names to match yours.

```ts
interface Ride {
  id: string;
  startedAt: Date;
  endedAt: Date | null;
  timeZone: string;            // IANA, e.g. "America/Chicago"
  currency: string;            // ISO 4217, e.g. "USD"
  startLocation?: string;
  endLocation?: string;
  distanceMeters?: number;

  // All money in minor units (cents), as already computed at ride end
  unlockFeeCents: number;
  perMinuteRateCents: number;
  billedMinutes: number;
  discountCents: number;       // positive number, subtracted
  taxCents: number;
  totalCents: number;
}

interface Receipt {
  subject: string;
  text: string;
  html: string;
}

export function buildReceipt(ride: Ride): Receipt {
  if (!ride.endedAt) {
    throw new Error(`Cannot build receipt for unfinished ride ${ride.id}`);
  }

  const money = (cents: number) =>
    new Intl.NumberFormat("en-US", { style: "currency", currency: ride.currency })
      .format(cents / 100);

  const dateTime = (d: Date) =>
    new Intl.DateTimeFormat("en-US", {
      dateStyle: "medium",
      timeStyle: "short",
      timeZone: ride.timeZone,
    }).format(d);

  const rideCostCents = ride.perMinuteRateCents * ride.billedMinutes;

  const lines: { label: string; amount: string }[] = [
    { label: "Unlock fee", amount: money(ride.unlockFeeCents) },
    {
      label: `Ride time (${ride.billedMinutes} min × ${money(ride.perMinuteRateCents)})`,
      amount: money(rideCostCents),
    },
  ];
  if (ride.discountCents > 0) {
    lines.push({ label: "Discount", amount: `-${money(ride.discountCents)}` });
  }
  lines.push({ label: "Tax", amount: money(ride.taxCents) });

  // Guard: the receipt must agree with what the customer was actually charged.
  const expectedTotal =
    ride.unlockFeeCents + rideCostCents - ride.discountCents + ride.taxCents;
  if (expectedTotal !== ride.totalCents) {
    throw new Error(
      `Receipt total mismatch for ride ${ride.id}: computed ${expectedTotal}, recorded ${ride.totalCents}`
    );
  }

  const details: { label: string; value: string }[] = [
    { label: "Ride ID", value: ride.id },
    { label: "Started", value: dateTime(ride.startedAt) },
    { label: "Ended", value: dateTime(ride.endedAt) },
  ];
  if (ride.startLocation) details.push({ label: "From", value: ride.startLocation });
  if (ride.endLocation) details.push({ label: "To", value: ride.endLocation });
  if (ride.distanceMeters != null) {
    details.push({
      label: "Distance",
      value: `${(ride.distanceMeters / 1000).toFixed(2)} km`,
    });
  }

  const subject = `Your receipt for ${dateTime(ride.endedAt)} ride – ${money(ride.totalCents)}`;

  const text = [
    "Thanks for riding with us!",
    "",
    ...details.map((d) => `${d.label}: ${d.value}`),
    "",
    ...lines.map((l) => `${l.label}: ${l.amount}`),
    `Total: ${money(ride.totalCents)}`,
  ].join("\n");

  const esc = (s: string) =>
    s.replace(/&/g, "&amp;").replace(/</g, "&lt;").replace(/>/g, "&gt;")
     .replace(/"/g, "&quot;").replace(/'/g, "&#39;");

  const html = `
<div style="font-family: sans-serif; max-width: 480px; margin: 0 auto;">
  <h2>Thanks for riding with us!</h2>
  <table style="width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; margin-bottom:16px;">
    ${details
      .map((d) => `<tr><td style="color:#666;padding:2px 0;">${esc(d.label)}</td><td style="text-align:right;">${esc(d.value)}</td></tr>`)
      .join("\n    ")}
  </table>
  <table style="width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; border-top:1px solid #ddd;">
    ${lines
      .map((l) => `<tr><td style="padding:4px 0;">${esc(l.label)}</td><td style="text-align:right;">${esc(l.amount)}</td></tr>`)
      .join("\n    ")}
    <tr style="font-weight:bold; border-top:1px solid #ddd;">
      <td style="padding-top:8px;">Total</td>
      <td style="text-align:right; padding-top:8px;">${esc(money(ride.totalCents))}</td>
    </tr>
  </table>
</div>`.trim();

  return { subject, text, html };
}
```

**Design choices**
- **It's pure.** It takes a ride and returns `{subject, text, html}`, with no sending and no DB access, so it's easy to test. The send step can be a separate function.
- **It doesn't recompute pricing.** It formats the amounts already stored on the ride and throws if they don't add up to `totalCents`. That keeps a receipt from disagreeing with the actual charge, but if you'd rather not fail on a mismatch, log it instead.
- **Money stays in integer cents** until formatting, and times are rendered in the ride's time zone, not the server's.
- **Both plain text and HTML are returned**, since most email APIs want a multipart message. User-supplied strings like location names are HTML-escaped.

**Things to check against your setup**
- If you have multiple tax lines, a pause/parking fee, or a different pricing model (per-km, flat passes), the `lines` array is the place to extend.
- The locale is hardcoded to `en-US`. If you support other languages, pass in a locale.
- When you wire up sending, make it idempotent, for example by storing a `receiptSentAt` on the ride, so retries on ride-end events don't send duplicates.

